WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.400 --> 00:00:07.511
Your body has parts, and
every part has a name.

2
00:00:07.731 --> 00:00:11.168
You have five senses, and
they tell you about the world.

3
00:00:11.668 --> 00:00:14.919
Find each part on the child.
Touch it on yourself too.

4
00:00:15.139 --> 00:00:17.461
Your head is at the top of your body.

5
00:00:17.681 --> 00:00:21.303
Your arms come out from your
shoulders. Your hands are at the end.

6
00:00:21.523 --> 00:00:23.752
Your tummy is in the middle of your body.

7
00:00:23.972 --> 00:00:27.780
Your legs are underneath. Your
feet are at the end of your legs.

8
00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:31.623
On your face are your eyes, your
ears, your nose and your mouth.

9
00:00:31.843 --> 00:00:34.211
Most people have all of these parts.

10
00:00:34.711 --> 00:00:38.519
You have five senses. Each
one uses a part of your body.

11
00:00:38.739 --> 00:00:42.408
Sight: your eyes see
colours, shapes and light.

12
00:00:42.628 --> 00:00:46.157
Hearing: your ears hear
sounds, loud and quiet.

13
00:00:46.377 --> 00:00:49.907
Smell: your nose smells
bread baking, and flowers.

14
00:00:50.127 --> 00:00:54.028
Taste: your tongue tastes
sweet, salty and sour things.

15
00:00:54.248 --> 00:00:58.381
Touch: your skin feels hot,
cold, rough and smooth.

16
00:00:58.601 --> 00:01:02.177
Touch is not only your hands.
Your skin is all over you.

17
00:01:02.677 --> 00:01:06.299
Your senses tell you about the
world, and they keep you safe.

18
00:01:06.519 --> 00:01:09.073
Listen! Your ears hear a car coming.

19
00:01:09.293 --> 00:01:12.173
Your nose smells smoke,
before you see the fire.

20
00:01:12.393 --> 00:01:15.922
Your skin feels that a cup is
too hot, before it burns you.

21
00:01:16.422 --> 00:01:20.184
Look at four friends:
Amal, Sami, Nora and Omar.

22
00:01:20.404 --> 00:01:24.490
Most people have two eyes. Some
eyes are brown and some are green.

23
00:01:24.710 --> 00:01:29.401
Most people have hair. Some hair
is curly and some is straight.

24
00:01:29.621 --> 00:01:33.800
Different does not mean better or
worse. It just means not the same.

25
00:01:34.020 --> 00:01:36.482
So we are alike, and we are different.

26
00:01:36.982 --> 00:01:40.279
Long ago, people measured
with their hands and feet.

27
00:01:40.499 --> 00:01:43.935
A hand span is from your
thumb to your little finger.

28
00:01:44.155 --> 00:01:48.010
Put a hand at the feet. Keep
going to the top of the head.

29
00:01:48.230 --> 00:01:52.038
Amal is nine hand spans
tall. Write it in a table.

30
00:01:52.258 --> 00:01:57.831
Sami is ten, and Nora is eight. Ten
is the most, so Sami is tallest.

31
00:01:58.331 --> 00:02:01.814
You know the parts of your body,
from your head to your feet.

32
00:02:02.034 --> 00:02:05.703
Five senses tell you about the
world, and they keep you safe.

33
00:02:05.923 --> 00:02:10.659
People are alike and different.
You can measure them in hand spans.

34
00:02:10.879 --> 00:02:13.201
Clap your hands. You know your body!
